#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid "A note on output"
msgstr "Napomena o izlazu"

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"goat is built to be both a pleasure to use _and_ safe to script. Friendly "
"touches — a 🐐 when everything's green, a hint about your next step — only "
"ever appear on an interactive terminal. Pipe goat into a script or ask for "
"`--json` and you get clean, stable, machine-readable output with nothing "
"decorative in the way. Set `GOAT_NO_FUN=1` and even the interactive "
"flourishes go quiet."
msgstr ""
"goat je izrađen tako da bude i ugodan za korištenje _i_ siguran za "
"skriptiranje. Prijateljski detalji — 🐐 kad je sve zeleno, savjet o "
"sljedećem koraku — pojavljuju se isključivo na interaktivnom terminalu. "
"Provedite goat kroz skriptu (pipe) ili zatražite `--json` i dobit ćete čist, "
"stabilan, strojno čitljiv izlaz bez ičega dekorativnog na putu. Postavite "
"`GOAT_NO_FUN=1` i čak i interaktivni ukrasi utihnu."

#: src/getting-started.md:3
msgid ""
"You don't need a profile, a bundle, or a network to start. goat ships with a "
"sandbox so you can learn by doing, safely."
msgstr ""
"Za početak vam ne trebaju profil, bundle ni mreža. goat dolazi sa sandboxom "
"pa možete učiti radeći, sigurno."

#: src/getting-started.md:5
msgid "1. Say hello"
msgstr "1. Pozdravite"

#: src/getting-started.md:11
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulated fabric, no real mesh. Run `goat init` to attach a real "
"env.\n"
"goat hello — saying `lo` to the fabric as `default` on topic `hello/"
"default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     accepted topic `hello/default` (simulated)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     routed `lo` to `hello/default` over the WireGuard "
"P2P path (simulated)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber your subscriber received `lo` — round-trip complete "
"(simulated)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: the first message ever sent over a network (ARPANET, 29 Oct 1969) "
"— they typed \"LOGIN\" and the link crashed after two letters.\n"
"round-trip complete.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulirani fabric, nema stvarnog mesha. Pokrenite `goat init` za "
"priključenje stvarnog okruženja.\n"
"goat hello — govorim `lo` fabricu kao `default` na topicu `hello/default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     prihvatio topic `hello/default` (simulirano)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     usmjerio `lo` na `hello/default` preko WireGuard P2P "
"puta (simulirano)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber vaš pretplatnik primio je `lo` — povratno putovanje "
"dovršeno (simulirano)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: prva poruka ikad poslana preko mreže (ARPANET, 29. lis. 1969.) — "
"utipkali su \"LOGIN\" i veza se srušila nakon dva slova.\n"
"povratno putovanje dovršeno.\n"
"```"

#: src/getting-started.md:21
msgid ""
"`goat hello` publishes a message, subscribes to it, and watches it come back "
"— narrating every hop the data took. In the sandbox those hops are "
"simulated; against a real env they're real. Either way, when it says _round-"
"trip complete_, you know the path works end to end."
msgstr ""
"`goat hello` objavljuje poruku, pretplaćuje se na nju i prati kako se vraća "
"— opisujući svaki skok koji su podaci napravili. U sandboxu su ti skokovi "
"simulirani; nad stvarnim okruženjem su stvarni. U svakom slučaju, kad kaže "
"_povratno putovanje dovršeno_, znate da put radi od kraja do kraja."

#: src/getting-started.md:23
msgid ""
"The message is `lo` on purpose — the first thing ever sent over a network."
msgstr "Poruka je namjerno `lo` — prva stvar ikad poslana preko mreže."

#: src/getting-started.md:25
msgid "2. Take the tour"
msgstr "2. Krenite u obilazak"

#: src/getting-started.md:31
msgid ""
"`goat tutor` is a self-paced, hands-on tour — think `vimtutor` for the "
"fabric. Eight short lessons take you from \"what is this\" to publishing, "
"subscribing, diagnosing, and reading the substrate cascade. It runs in the "
"sandbox by default, saves your place, and you can stop and resume any time:"
msgstr ""
"`goat tutor` je praktičan obilazak vlastitim tempom — zamislite `vimtutor` "
"za fabric. Osam kratkih lekcija vodi vas od \"što je ovo\" do objavljivanja, "
"pretplate, dijagnosticiranja i čitanja kaskade substrata. Po zadanom se "
"izvodi u sandboxu, sprema vašu poziciju, a možete ga zaustaviti i nastaviti "
"bilo kada:"

#: src/getting-started.md:39
msgid "3. Attach a real environment"
msgstr "3. Priključite stvarno okruženje"

#: src/getting-started.md:41
msgid ""
"When you've been issued an onboarding **bundle** (a `.cbor` file with your "
"identity), the wizard takes it from here:"
msgstr ""
"Kad vam je izdan onboarding **bundle** (`.cbor` datoteka s vašim "
"identitetom), čarobnjak preuzima dalje:"

#: src/getting-started.md:49
msgid ""
"`goat init` is the friendly front door — it detects whether you're set up, "
"lets you choose the sandbox or a real env, proves it works, and points you "
"at the tutor. `goat doctor` then runs a stepped reachability check (mesh → "
"router → certificate → portal) and, if anything's wrong, tells you exactly "
"what to fix."
msgstr ""
"`goat init` je prijateljska ulazna vrata — otkriva jeste li postavljeni, "
"omogućuje vam odabir sandboxa ili stvarnog okruženja, dokazuje da radi i "
"upućuje vas na tutora. `goat doctor` zatim provodi postupnu provjeru "
"dosežnosti (mesh → router → certifikat → portal) i, ako nešto nije u redu, "
"točno vam kaže što popraviti."

#: src/getting-started.md:51
msgid ""
"When all of doctor's steps pass, you'll see a small 🐐 — you're on the "
"fabric."
msgstr "Kad svi koraci doctora prođu, vidjet ćete malu 🐐 — na fabricu ste."

#: src/getting-started.md:53
msgid "Where to next"
msgstr "Kamo dalje"

#: src/getting-started.md:55
msgid "New to the ideas? Read **[How the fabric works](concepts.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Novi ste u ovim idejama? Pročitajte **[Kako fabric radi](concepts.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:56
msgid "Ready to do things? Jump to **[Everyday tasks](everyday.md)**."
msgstr "Spremni za rad? Skočite na **[Svakodnevni zadaci](everyday.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:57
msgid "Something not working? **[Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md)**."
msgstr "Nešto ne radi? **[Rješavanje problema](troubleshooting.md)**."

#: src/concepts.md:3
msgid ""
"You can use goat productively with just three ideas: **identity**, "
"**topics**, and **no broker**. Here they are."
msgstr ""
"goat možete produktivno koristiti uz samo tri ideje: **identitet**, "
"**topici** i **bez brokera**. Evo ih."

#: src/concepts.md:5
msgid "A mesh you join with an identity"
msgstr "Mesh kojem se pridružujete s identitetom"

#: src/concepts.md:7
msgid ""
"The fabric is a self-healing mesh. Peers connect **directly** to each other "
"over encrypted WireGuard tunnels — once you're enrolled, your data doesn't "
"route through a central server, and your connections survive a management-"
"plane outage or a flaky uplink."
msgstr ""
"Fabric je samoizlječivi mesh. Čvorovi (peers) se povezuju **izravno** jedan "
"s drugim preko šifriranih WireGuard tunela — nakon što ste upisani, vaši "
"podaci ne prolaze kroz središnji poslužitelj, a vaše veze preživljavaju "
"ispad upravljačke ravnine ili nestabilan uplink."

#: src/concepts.md:9
msgid ""
"You join with an **identity**: an onboarding _bundle_ that carries your "
"certificate, an access token, and where the fabric lives. The fabric admits "
"you by _who you are_, not by a shared password. `goat profile init "
"<bundle.cbor>` installs that identity; you can hold several under different "
"_contexts_ and switch between them."
msgstr ""
"Pridružujete se s **identitetom**: onboarding _bundleom_ koji nosi vaš "
"certifikat, pristupni token i mjesto gdje fabric živi. Fabric vas prima na "
"temelju _tko ste_, a ne dijeljene lozinke. `goat profile init <bundle.cbor>` "
"instalira taj identitet; možete ih držati nekoliko pod različitim "
"_kontekstima_ i prebacivati se između njih."

#: src/concepts.md:19
msgid "Topics: publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Topici: objavljivanje i pretplata"

#: src/concepts.md:21
msgid ""
"Data moves on **topics** — slash-delimited paths like `acme/radar1/tracks`. "
"The model is publish/subscribe:"
msgstr ""
"Podaci se kreću po **topicima** — putanjama odijeljenim kosom crtom poput "
"`acme/radar1/tracks`. Model je objavljivanje/pretplata (publish/subscribe):"

#: src/concepts.md:23
msgid "**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) writes a value to a topic."
msgstr "**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) upisuje vrijednost u topic."

#: src/concepts.md:24
msgid ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) receives every value published there, "
"live, as long as you're allowed to read it."
msgstr ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) prima svaku vrijednost objavljenu ondje, "
"uživo, sve dok ju smijete čitati."

#: src/concepts.md:26
msgid ""
"A topic is just a name; you create it (`goat topic create`), publish to it, "
"and anyone permitted can subscribe. `goat hello` is simply a publish and a "
"subscribe wired together so you can watch a value make the round trip."
msgstr ""
"Topic je samo naziv; kreirate ga (`goat topic create`), objavljujete na "
"njega, a svatko tko ima dopuštenje može se pretplatiti. `goat hello` je "
"jednostavno objava i pretplata povezane zajedno kako biste mogli pratiti "
"vrijednost kako odrađuje povratno putovanje."

#: src/concepts.md:28
msgid "No broker — and why that matters"
msgstr "Bez brokera — i zašto je to važno"

#: src/concepts.md:30
msgid ""
"There is **no central broker** sitting in the middle of the data path. When "
"you publish, the value flows over the mesh directly to the peers subscribed "
"to it. That's deliberate: it removes the single bottleneck and single point "
"of failure that a broker would be."
msgstr ""
"Ne postoji **središnji broker** koji sjedi usred podatkovnog puta. Kad "
"objavite, vrijednost teče preko mesha izravno do čvorova pretplaćenih na "
"nju. To je namjerno: uklanja jedinstveno usko grlo i jedinstvenu točku kvara "
"koje bi broker predstavljao."

#: src/concepts.md:32
msgid ""
"A practical consequence: **reads are broad, writes are the cut.** Being able "
"to _read_ a topic is permissive by design; _writing_ to one is governed by "
"your identity. So you'll rarely be surprised by what you can subscribe to, "
"and the integrity of what's published is anchored to who published it."
msgstr ""
"Praktična posljedica: **čitanja su široka, upisi su rez.** Mogućnost "
"_čitanja_ topica je po dizajnu dopuštajuća; _upisivanje_ u njega uređeno je "
"vašim identitetom. Tako rijetko ćete biti iznenađeni onime na što se možete "
"pretplatiti, a integritet onoga što je objavljeno usidren je u to tko ga je "
"objavio."

#: src/concepts.md:34
msgid "Sandbox vs. real"
msgstr "Sandbox naspram stvarnog"

#: src/concepts.md:36
msgid ""
"Everything above has a faithful **in-process simulation** — the sandbox. "
"`goat hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox`, and `goat tutor` exercise the "
"same shapes (a topic, a publish, a round-trip, a verdict) with no network "
"and no identity, so you can learn the model before you touch the real "
"fabric. The sandbox always says so with a `◇ SANDBOX` banner, and it never "
"writes to or reads from a real mesh."
msgstr ""
"Sve gore navedeno ima vjernu **in-process simulaciju** — sandbox. `goat "
"hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox` i `goat tutor` izvode iste oblike "
"(topic, objavu, povratno putovanje, presudu) bez mreže i bez identiteta, pa "
"možete naučiti model prije nego što dotaknete stvarni fabric. Sandbox to "
"uvijek naznačuje `◇ SANDBOX` natpisom i nikada ne piše u stvarni mesh niti "
"čita iz njega."

#: src/concepts.md:38
msgid ""
"When you switch to a real env, the _commands don't change_ — only the "
"backing does."
msgstr ""
"Kad se prebacite na stvarno okruženje, _naredbe se ne mijenjaju_ — mijenja "
"se samo pozadina."

#: src/concepts.md:40
msgid ""
"Want the deeper architecture (the relay fallback, the access model, the "
"audit trail)? Ask your goat administrator for the design references — this "
"guide stays focused on operating the CLI."
msgstr ""
"Želite dublju arhitekturu (rezervni relay, model pristupa, revizijski trag)? "
"Zatražite od svog goat administratora projektne reference — ovaj se vodič "
"usredotočuje na rad s CLI-jem."

#: src/everyday.md:3
msgid ""
"The commands you'll actually reach for, as quick recipes. Add `--help` to "
"any of them for the full set of flags, or see the **[Command reference]"
"(reference.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Naredbe za kojima ćete zaista posezati, kao brzi recepti. Dodajte `--help` "
"bilo kojoj od njih za potpuni skup zastavica ili pogledajte **[Referencu "
"naredbi](reference.md)**."

#: src/everyday.md:5
msgid "Check you're connected"
msgstr "Provjerite jeste li povezani"

#: src/everyday.md:12
msgid ""
"`goat doctor` is your first stop whenever something feels off — each step "
"that fails prints a specific remediation. When everything's green, both "
"commands give you a clear all-clear."
msgstr ""
"`goat doctor` je vaša prva postaja kad god se nešto čini neispravnim — svaki "
"korak koji ne uspije ispisuje specifičan postupak otklanjanja. Kad je sve "
"zeleno, obje naredbe daju vam jasan znak da je sve u redu."

#: src/everyday.md:14
msgid "Publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Objavljivanje i pretplata"

#: src/everyday.md:16
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # watch a topic live (Ctrl-C to "
"stop)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # a whole subtree\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # publish a payload\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # gledajte topic uživo (Ctrl-C za "
"prekid)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # cijelo podstablo\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # objavite sadržaj (payload)\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:22
msgid "Want to see the ripple a publish sets off? Add `--narrate`:"
msgstr "Želite vidjeti valove koje objava izaziva? Dodajte `--narrate`:"

#: src/everyday.md:24
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:28
msgid "Work with topics"
msgstr "Rad s topicima"

#: src/everyday.md:30
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # list topics\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # drill into an org/prefix\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # one topic's full record\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # ispiši topice\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # uđi u organizaciju/prefiks\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # potpuni zapis jednog topica\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:37
msgid ""
"After you create a topic, goat nudges you toward the natural next step "
"(watch it, or publish to it)."
msgstr ""
"Nakon što kreirate topic, goat vas usmjerava prema prirodnom sljedećem "
"koraku (gledajte ga ili objavljujte na njega)."

#: src/everyday.md:39
msgid "Diagnose a problem"
msgstr "Dijagnosticirajte problem"

#: src/everyday.md:47
msgid ""
"`inspect` returns findings and the remedy for each — what's wrong and what "
"to do about it."
msgstr ""
"`inspect` vraća nalaze i lijek za svaki od njih — što nije u redu i što "
"učiniti u vezi s tim."

#: src/everyday.md:49
msgid "Scripting"
msgstr "Skriptiranje"

#: src/everyday.md:51
msgid ""
"Every command that prints a human view also offers `--json` for a stable, "
"machine-readable one. The JSON form never carries banners, hints, or "
"flourishes, and its shape and your exit code stay constant across releases "
"and languages:"
msgstr ""
"Svaka naredba koja ispisuje ljudski prikaz nudi i `--json` za stabilan, "
"strojno čitljiv prikaz. JSON oblik nikada ne nosi natpise, savjete ni "
"ukrase, a njegov oblik i vaš izlazni kod ostaju nepromijenjeni kroz izdanja "
"i jezike:"

#: src/everyday.md:58
msgid "This is the contract: **friendly on a terminal, clean in a pipe.**"
msgstr "Ovo je ugovor: **prijateljski na terminalu, čist u pipeu.**"

#: src/everyday.md:60
msgid ""
"One caution: `goat status` opens a real session at the router each time it runs, so it is a check you run when you want an answer, not something to poll from a timer. For a trend over time use `goat health` or `goat top`, which read what the goatnet already publishes."
msgstr ""
"Jedno upozorenje: `goat status` pri svakom pokretanju otvara stvarnu sesiju prema usmjerivaču, pa je to provjera koju pokrećete kad želite odgovor, a ne nešto što se poziva iz timera. Za trend kroz vrijeme koristite `goat health` ili `goat top`, koji čitaju ono što goatnet već objavljuje."

#: src/install.md:3
msgid ""
"goat is a single self-contained binary — no runtime, no dependencies. It's "
"served mesh-internally from `get.<your-goatnet>` (you're already on the mesh "
"if you can read this), and the version here always matches the binary that "
"surface serves."
msgstr ""
"goat je jedan samostalan binarni program — bez runtimea, bez ovisnosti. "
"Poslužuje se interno unutar mesha s `get.<your-goatnet>` (već ste na meshu "
"ako ovo možete pročitati), a ovdje navedena verzija uvijek odgovara binarnom "
"programu koji ta površina poslužuje."

#: src/install.md:5
msgid "Quick install"
msgstr "Brza instalacija"

#: src/install.md:7
msgid "**macOS / Linux**"
msgstr "**macOS / Linux**"

#: src/install.md:10
msgid ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"

#: src/install.md:11
msgid "$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"

#: src/install.md:12
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:17
msgid "Make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your `PATH`."
msgstr "Provjerite da je `~/.local/bin` na vašem `PATH`-u."

#: src/install.md:19
msgid "**Windows (PowerShell)**"
msgstr "**Windows (PowerShell)**"

#: src/install.md:21
msgid ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"

#: src/install.md:26
msgid ""
"Every subcommand works on Windows except `goat client` (the local tunnel "
"daemon), which is Linux/macOS-only."
msgstr ""
"Svaka podnaredba radi na Windowsu osim `goat client` (lokalni daemon za "
"tunel), koji je dostupan samo na Linuxu/macOS-u."

#: src/install.md:28
msgid "Verify the download (recommended)"
msgstr "Provjerite preuzimanje (preporučeno)"

#: src/install.md:30
msgid ""
"The download surface publishes a per-binary `*.sha256` and an aggregate "
"`SHA256SUMS`. For a high-assurance install, verify before you run:"
msgstr ""
"Površina za preuzimanje objavljuje `*.sha256` po binarnom programu i skupni "
"`SHA256SUMS`. Za instalaciju visoke pouzdanosti, provjerite prije pokretanja:"

#: src/install.md:33
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""

#: src/install.md:34
msgid "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"
msgstr "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"

#: src/install.md:41
msgid "Platforms"
msgstr "Platforme"

#: src/install.md:43
msgid "OS"
msgstr "OS"

#: src/install.md:43
msgid "Architectures"
msgstr "Arhitekture"

